WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.865
<i>Something's got a hold of me lately.</i>

2
00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>No. I don't know myself anymore.</i>

3
00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.958
<i>Feels like the walls Are all closin' in.</i>

4
00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:28.254
<i>And the devil's knockin' at my door.</i>

5
00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.547
<i>Whoa.</i>

6
00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:33.217
<i>Out of my mind
How many times did I tell you</i>

7
00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:36.971
<i>I'm fallin' apart Right in front of you.</i>

8
00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:39.181
<i>Can't you see?</i>

9
00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:46.105
<i>I lose control.</i>

10
00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:50.341
<i>When you're not here with me.</i>

11
00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.779
<i>Yeah. you're breakin' my heart. baby.</i>

12
00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:58.701
<i>You make a mess of me.</i>

13
00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.661
Nobody even knows where he went.

14
00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:03.372
After that dinner. I can't say I blame him.

15
00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.708
Heard he saddled Duke
with a full pack and just took off.

16
00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.900
Weird.

17
00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:10.588
Please tell me we are not
still talking about that man.

18
00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:11.881
Staten is Staten.

19
00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:15.718
Trying to figure out what's going on
under that hood's like falling up a tree.

20
00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.386
It's impossible and dumb.

21
00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.931
It isn't like him to just up
and abandon his ranch like that. though.

22
00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.917
Are you kidding me?
Retreating is Staten's go-to move.

23
00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.294
You know who doesn't retreat?

24
00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:32.693
Make him stay.

25
00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:35.863
He's like 20 festival planners in…

26
00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:37.972
One perfect body.

27
00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.476
He has shown up in every way.

28
00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:44.436
Gave me this foot rub last night.

29
00:01:45.688 --> 00:01:49.585
Was it a "marry me" foot rub?
Come on. am I right or am I right?

30
00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.361
- I mean…
- You're right.

31
00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.864
He deserves an answer.
and I'm giving him one.

32
00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.118
As soon as I know what that is.

33
00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.887
Girl…

34
00:01:59.911 --> 00:02:04.517
He's asking me to choose between
an amazing city that I love and my home.

35
00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:06.727
You expect me to up and leave Ransom?

36
00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:08.461
We just want you to be happy.

37
00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:12.024
Ange. El.

38
00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:13.466
- Hi.
- We good?

39
00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:15.885
We good.

40
00:02:16.886 --> 00:02:19.115
- Hey.
- Hi. What's this?

41
00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.033
I'm stealing you away for a date.

42
00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:22.433
That's sweet.

43
00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:25.955
But I have… I have to go through
the tips from last week.

44
00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.081
I have.

45
00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:29.023
She has.

46
00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:32.837
Okay. Well. I also have
a vendor call that...

47
00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:36.114
- Has been made.
- Already been made.

48
00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.117
You guys…

49
00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:44.247
Okay. Well. I guess
I'm yours. sir. Steal away.

50
00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:45.915
Stolen.

51
00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.029
What do you think?

52
00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:01.240
I think you're making Quinn's job easy.

53
00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:02.681
It's your best yet. babe.

54
00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:07.329
I feel like it's missing something.

55
00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.147
I think you're nuts.

56
00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:11.858
Like here?

57
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.676
So you guys are… You…

58
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.970
You're like really not talking. Cool.

59
00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:26.056
Anything I say gets run straight up
the ladder to Daddy Staten.

60
00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.392
I don't feel like getting
into more shit with my boss.

61
00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:30.311
His boss. the total scumbag.

62
00:03:30.335 --> 00:03:33.022
Lauren. could you remind your boyfriend

63
00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.548
I only took this job to support his future?

64
00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:39.612
Also. don't finish the cereal
and put it back on the shelf.

65
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:42.740
Fine. Maybe tell him
to get his outdoor cat out of my closet.

66
00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:45.618
Says more about your disgusting
closet than it does about my cat.

67
00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.578
Y'all. enough.

68
00:03:47.602 --> 00:03:49.622
Are you really not on my side here?

69
00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:52.750
It's hard to be on a side
when you're both acting like children.

70
00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:53.775
Fine.

71
00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.736
I'm going to get some air.

72
00:04:04.535 --> 00:04:05.954
I like the musician. …

73
00:04:06.537 --> 00:04:08.015
Where's the cowboy?

74
00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:10.083
I think it's a little on the nose.

75
00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:23.739
This is fun. Where are we going?

76
00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.950
Wouldn't be much
of a secret if I told you.

77
00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:27.684
I guess not.

78
00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.668
You did not just bust that lock!

79
00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:38.254
Sure I did.
It's why I borrowed your bolt cutters.

80
00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.090
- Are you serious?
- No. that's how I found it.

81
00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.801
This feels very illegal.

82
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:45.052
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

83
00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:47.870
Well. it's good to be
a little naughty sometimes.

84
00:04:48.538 --> 00:04:49.580
So…

85
00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.268
What do you think?

86
00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.085
This is the Lone Star Theater.

87
00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:57.314
I haven't been here
since it closed years ago.

88
00:04:57.338 --> 00:04:59.692
I can't believe it's been sitting empty.

89
00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:02.778
A few people tried.
but bringing it back up to code

90
00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.823
is just too big of a challenge.

91
00:05:05.847 --> 00:05:07.181
Yeah. it's a shame.

92
00:05:08.516 --> 00:05:10.160
Wait right here. okay?

93
00:05:10.184 --> 00:05:11.227
Okay.

94
00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:27.577
God. it is still so beautiful.

95
00:05:29.912 --> 00:05:32.474
- How'd you find it?
- Ummm…

96
00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.583
Just

97
00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:35.894
poking around.

98
00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:37.754
Sneaky.

99
00:05:39.547 --> 00:05:41.841
God. my dad used to love this place.

100
00:05:43.468 --> 00:05:45.053
I had all my recitals here.

101
00:05:46.471 --> 00:05:48.532
My mom used to hang out in the back.

102
00:05:48.556 --> 00:05:50.975
but he'd always be right up front.

103
00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.022
And I'd be right there.

104
00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.694
I fell in love with music on that bench.

105
00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:06.032
Wait. this is where it all started?

106
00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:09.077
Well…

107
00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:12.473
Good thing I tuned it. then.

108
00:06:12.497 --> 00:06:14.374
No. you didn't.

109
00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:16.125
Yeah. I did.

110
00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:20.356
I mean. I knew it was special.
I just didn't know it was that special.

111
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.983
I've been sneaking in
all week just to hear it.

112
00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:24.133
And the acoustics?

113
00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.488
They're just out of this world.

114
00:06:27.512 --> 00:06:29.764
All right. go easy on me. yeah?

115
00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:32.475
Because I am no Quinn O'Grady.

116
00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:22.942
<i>Every little moment.</i>

117
00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:49.218
<i>Walk me through the garden.</i>

118
00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:54.891
<i>I wanna feel the earth.</i>

119
00:07:57.018 --> 00:07:59.979
<i>Back before we started.</i>

120
00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:05.902
<i>Back before it hurt.</i>

121
00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:27.798
<i>Every little moment.</i>

122
00:08:33.721 --> 00:08:36.974
<i>There are mountains in my mind.</i>

123
00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:44.333
<i>Well. I got my boots and my guitar.</i>

124
00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:47.151
<i>Yeah. I'm a bad mother-shut-your-mouth.</i>

125
00:08:51.656 --> 00:08:53.926
Well. look who's back.

126
00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.344
You been cheating on me. Sam?

127
00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.203
Never. Just doing business.

128
00:08:58.079 --> 00:09:01.642
I've got a pulled pork and a side
of hush puppies fired up for you.

129
00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:05.169
Thank you. darling.
And would you also get me a…

130
00:09:06.963 --> 00:09:11.068
Ellie. if I didn't know better. I'd say
you're warming up to old Sam Kirkland.

131
00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:14.613
No. you don't know better.
You order the same damn thing every day.

132
00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:16.722
Well. let's make it a whiskey. too.

133
00:09:17.765 --> 00:09:19.267
Must've been a good trip.

134
00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:22.228
It was. Yes. it was.

135
00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:25.815
So. one Kirkland goes
and another comes in.

136
00:09:26.315 --> 00:09:29.360
Ain't enough room in this town. I guess.

137
00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:34.490
It looks like that board vote
is going to go your way then.

138
00:09:35.157 --> 00:09:38.595
That's where you were.

139
00:09:38.619 --> 00:09:40.580
Locking in your backers. Okay.

140
00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:43.958
I got what I needed. except one.

141
00:09:46.002 --> 00:09:47.980
Hell. I ain't worried.

142
00:09:48.004 --> 00:09:51.424
I just need one more big play
for the Double K.

143
00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:53.694
Well. shit.

144
00:09:53.718 --> 00:09:57.948
Good trip. indeed. I say that calls
for a Johnnie Walker Blue.

145
00:09:57.972 --> 00:09:59.890
Make it two. one for you.

146
00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:02.077
You know I'd love to.

147
00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:05.080
I know. I'll drink them both.

148
00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:06.981
Just give me a cheers. would you?

149
00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.863
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

150
00:10:19.076 --> 00:10:22.264
This bitch is good.
I knew she could hook him.

151
00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:23.581
I won the bet.

152
00:10:25.082 --> 00:10:26.226
You bet against me?

153
00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:27.501
No. I didn't.

154
00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:31.356
Okay. So what now?

155
00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.548
We move on him?

156
00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:36.612
No. I say we give it a few more days
just to be safe.

157
00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:40.115
- And miss our window? Are you crazy?
- It does feel like a window.

158
00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:42.868
He seems emotional. cocky.

159
00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:45.353
He's greased. Yancy. It's now.

160
00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.498
Where are you going?

161
00:10:48.522 --> 00:10:49.899
To call the Grease Man.

162
00:10:54.278 --> 00:10:56.381
Didn't think I'd get him to open up?

163
00:10:56.405 --> 00:10:57.740
No. I just…

164
00:10:59.241 --> 00:11:02.411
Look. this is the point of no return. okay?

165
00:11:03.287 --> 00:11:05.748
It's all going well now. but I just. I…

166
00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:08.084
What? What's wrong?

167
00:11:11.545 --> 00:11:13.690
Holy shit. He's kicking.

168
00:11:13.714 --> 00:11:16.384
- Or she's kicking.
- He's kicking. she's kicking.

169
00:11:19.762 --> 00:11:21.722
You should probably kiss me now.

170
00:11:34.985 --> 00:11:36.195
Breathtaking.

171
00:11:40.157 --> 00:11:41.534
Mural's not bad. either.

172
00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:47.915
I get the pull of this place now.

173
00:11:48.582 --> 00:11:51.269
I do. It's… It's part of you.

174
00:11:51.293 --> 00:11:52.628
It's your home.

175
00:11:53.212 --> 00:11:57.967
If this is where you see your life. then…
this is where I see mine.

176
00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:02.722
You'd…

177
00:12:03.806 --> 00:12:05.057
You'd move here?

178
00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:10.730
Well. I've just got to buy
a pair of boots. but…

179
00:12:14.608 --> 00:12:16.152
Just say yes.

180
00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.510
- But you can't. can you?
- Oliver...

181
00:12:23.534 --> 00:12:25.929
No. Quinn. I… I've waited.

182
00:12:25.953 --> 00:12:28.974
- You can't look past Staten.
- Don't make this about...

183
00:12:28.998 --> 00:12:30.416
How is it not about him?

184
00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:32.334
It's always about him.

185
00:12:33.043 --> 00:12:36.714
And it always will be. You know.
you're such an honest person.

186
00:12:37.673 --> 00:12:40.843
And yet. you won't be honest
with me. and worst of all.

187
00:12:41.343 --> 00:12:43.345
you won't be honest with yourself.

188
00:12:59.862 --> 00:13:02.966
I didn't realize ranching was a desk job.

189
00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.302
Think it was all bandits and moonshine?

190
00:13:05.326 --> 00:13:06.327
Yeah. kind of.

191
00:13:08.078 --> 00:13:10.223
Sorry. I'm looking for Lucas.

192
00:13:10.247 --> 00:13:12.976
Let me know when you find him.
He's out today.

193
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.210
Yeah. okay.

194
00:13:17.505 --> 00:13:19.924
- You were right. by the way.
- About what?

195
00:13:20.424 --> 00:13:22.986
My poster… needs a cowboy.

196
00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:27.365
… I don't know. It. feels
a little on the nose. don't you think?

197
00:13:27.389 --> 00:13:28.432
Funny.

198
00:13:30.518 --> 00:13:31.727
All right.

199
00:13:35.523 --> 00:13:36.941
I need a model.

200
00:13:40.152 --> 00:13:41.821
Can't draw it without a model.

201
00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:49.203
No. it's not happening. Brigman.

202
00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.372
Please.

203
00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.880
- Feel like I should be charging for this.
- Quiet. I'm doing your mouth. Hold on.

204
00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.319
I fucked up with Lucas.

205
00:14:04.343 --> 00:14:05.469
What do you mean?

206
00:14:06.387 --> 00:14:07.555
This whole…

207
00:14:08.973 --> 00:14:10.432
Divide at the ranch.

208
00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:16.604
Not his fault. He's just trying
to do right by Staten. I get it.

209
00:14:17.773 --> 00:14:20.150
Just don't want it
to become a thing between us.

210
00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.590
Why don't you… start small?

211
00:14:25.614 --> 00:14:28.033
Like. fix something that he cares about.

212
00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:31.036
Like his hair?

213
00:14:32.204 --> 00:14:36.542
No. I'm thinking more like.
get Mr. Scratch out of his closet.

214
00:14:45.509 --> 00:14:46.677
I think I got it.

215
00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:57.021
- Mouth looks a little messed up.
- Can it.

216
00:14:57.938 --> 00:15:00.232
Kidding. It's perfect.

217
00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:12.660
Ash.

218
00:15:14.371 --> 00:15:15.581
Your Highness.

219
00:15:16.415 --> 00:15:17.750
- I'll catch up.
- Yeah.

220
00:15:18.334 --> 00:15:20.604
You do know it's a Sunday. right?

221
00:15:20.628 --> 00:15:24.566
Yeah. I just… wanted to be somewhere
no one would find me.

222
00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.485
Why do you think I dragged the girls
through a Sunday practice?

223
00:15:27.509 --> 00:15:28.904
Who are you hiding from?

224
00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:32.866
My family. Jenny's back from college. Yay.

225
00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.308
It can't be all bad.

226
00:15:35.392 --> 00:15:37.245
You're the golden boy.

227
00:15:37.269 --> 00:15:40.564
When you're the less impressive sibling
in every way. it's hard to be around.

228
00:15:41.148 --> 00:15:44.944
Well. for what it's worth.
sibling trouble. sibling trouble.

229
00:15:46.987 --> 00:15:49.049
You hiding from Kit then?

230
00:15:49.073 --> 00:15:51.742
- Feels like I'm hiding from everybody.
- Even our girl?

231
00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:53.994
Even our girl.

232
00:15:54.662 --> 00:15:58.808
I have been trying so hard
to be there for her and support her.

233
00:15:58.832 --> 00:16:00.876
but she is just like…

234
00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:05.982
No. she has had a harder six months
than I could ever imagine. and...

235
00:16:06.006 --> 00:16:07.609
Stop.

236
00:16:07.633 --> 00:16:09.569
You get to feel feelings too.

237
00:16:09.593 --> 00:16:11.303
Yeah. no. I know. I just…

238
00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.099
Hard to explain. I guess.

239
00:16:16.058 --> 00:16:19.537
Sometimes I feel like
I can't be happy around Lauren.

240
00:16:19.561 --> 00:16:21.122
And you deserve to be.

241
00:16:21.146 --> 00:16:22.398
So do you.

242
00:16:22.898 --> 00:16:24.650
We should just enjoy it.

243
00:16:25.526 --> 00:16:27.236
How exactly do we do that?

244
00:16:28.195 --> 00:16:31.323
Maybe we start with this.

245
00:16:40.249 --> 00:16:42.918
<i>Don't you know time is always running.</i>

246
00:16:43.627 --> 00:16:44.813
Here. give me more.

247
00:16:44.837 --> 00:16:47.423
<i>That's something we can never change.</i>

248
00:16:49.925 --> 00:16:51.277
You sure this is okay?

249
00:16:51.301 --> 00:16:54.680
- Lucas. we're fine. My goodness.
- Yeah. you're right.

250
00:16:58.892 --> 00:17:01.746
Dude. you're unhinged right now.
Give it to me.

251
00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:05.500
- I just don't want to get us in trouble.
- <i>You'd</i> be getting us in trouble?

252
00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:08.253
I just know that you got
that UT scholarship.

253
00:17:08.277 --> 00:17:10.213
And it's a great opportunity.

254
00:17:10.237 --> 00:17:13.198
- What would happen if. you know?
- My God. stop.

255
00:17:14.116 --> 00:17:17.387
Do not add me to your list
of codependents. I don't want that.

256
00:17:17.411 --> 00:17:20.748
You can't take care of everything
for everybody. You know that?

257
00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.170
I'm just being real.

258
00:17:27.129 --> 00:17:29.465
You can't take care
of everything for Lauren.

259
00:17:31.091 --> 00:17:34.654
Maybe you just got to let her
figure her shit out on her own.

260
00:17:34.678 --> 00:17:36.430
Stop holding on so tight.

261
00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:39.117
I don't know.

262
00:17:39.141 --> 00:17:40.184
Yeah.

263
00:17:40.934 --> 00:17:42.519
Yeah. maybe you're right.

264
00:17:43.562 --> 00:17:44.563
Maybe.

265
00:17:45.564 --> 00:17:47.417
I'm also really high.

266
00:17:47.441 --> 00:17:50.819
Thank God. 'cause I am.
like. barely holding on right now.

267
00:18:00.996 --> 00:18:03.832
<i>Fall back on me.</i>

268
00:18:06.627 --> 00:18:08.629
Well. what do you think?

269
00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.609
You hate it.

270
00:18:12.633 --> 00:18:14.110
No. no. no. I don't hate it.

271
00:18:14.134 --> 00:18:15.886
I don't hate it at all. I…

272
00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:18.948
I love it.

273
00:18:18.972 --> 00:18:20.075
Really?

274
00:18:20.099 --> 00:18:22.226
Yeah. really. really. I love it.

275
00:18:24.353 --> 00:18:26.831
- … Are you okay then?
- Yeah. no. I'm okay.

276
00:18:26.855 --> 00:18:31.985
… Well. I'm not okay.
I'm in a bit of a fork in the road.

277
00:18:34.822 --> 00:18:36.949
Two paths ahead and I'm struggling.

278
00:18:38.325 --> 00:18:40.011
That probably sounds crazy.

279
00:18:40.035 --> 00:18:43.497
No. it doesn't. Trust me. not even a bit.

280
00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.184
Whoo. life's a trip?

281
00:18:46.208 --> 00:18:47.751
- Yeah.
- But. hey.

282
00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.438
- You killed it. kiddo.
- Really?

283
00:18:50.462 --> 00:18:53.316
- Yeah. Really. really.
- I couldn't have done it without you.

284
00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.610
No. I just encouraged you to submit.

285
00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:58.655
No. that's not true. You inspired me.

286
00:18:58.679 --> 00:19:02.242
Yeah. you've been carrying
this entire thing on your shoulders.

287
00:19:02.266 --> 00:19:06.687
I figured if you could do all that. then
I owed it to myself to create something.

288
00:19:07.896 --> 00:19:09.398
Thanks.

289
00:19:11.567 --> 00:19:14.027
- … Okay. I'll let you get to it.
- Yeah. okay.

290
00:19:15.779 --> 00:19:16.840
Hey. Lauren.

291
00:19:16.864 --> 00:19:17.865
Yeah?

292
00:19:19.032 --> 00:19:20.032
Thank you.

293
00:19:21.034 --> 00:19:22.202
Always.

294
00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:58.906
It's about damn time
you showed up. Levi.

295
00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:01.843
Starting to worry you got soft.

296
00:20:01.867 --> 00:20:04.244
What the hell are you doing here. Staten?

297
00:20:07.623 --> 00:20:10.167
Cooking dinner for my little brother.

298
00:20:21.803 --> 00:20:23.138
You look old.

299
00:20:23.972 --> 00:20:26.975
Thank you. You look like a goddamn hobo.

300
00:20:27.851 --> 00:20:29.162
Thank you.

301
00:20:29.186 --> 00:20:31.980
You're welcome. I almost forgot.

302
00:20:35.317 --> 00:20:36.419
Peanut M&M's.

303
00:20:36.443 --> 00:20:39.172
- That's right.
- Son of a bitch. man.

304
00:20:39.196 --> 00:20:40.364
And…

305
00:20:42.157 --> 00:20:43.408
{\an8}Some of the good stuff.

306
00:20:46.411 --> 00:20:47.663
So what do you want?

307
00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:53.519
It's been a while. I wanted to see you.

308
00:20:53.543 --> 00:20:55.396
- Saw you last fall.
- What fall?

309
00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:57.482
What. three years ago fall?

310
00:20:57.506 --> 00:21:01.027
When I was driving to Buc-ee's to grab
a Coke and you were siphoning gasoline?

311
00:21:01.051 --> 00:21:02.719
Was that three years ago?

312
00:21:05.264 --> 00:21:06.265
Here.

313
00:21:07.849 --> 00:21:09.392
How you been?

314
00:21:11.019 --> 00:21:12.062
Hanging in.

315
00:21:13.313 --> 00:21:14.773
I heard about your mom.

316
00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.168
Sorry I missed the funeral.

317
00:21:17.192 --> 00:21:19.236
There wasn't one.

318
00:21:26.159 --> 00:21:27.553
Sorry I missed Randall's.

319
00:21:27.577 --> 00:21:29.538
- Yeah.
- You…

320
00:21:31.999 --> 00:21:33.709
You doing okay with all that?

321
00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:35.294
Yeah.

322
00:21:35.877 --> 00:21:36.878
Yeah.

323
00:21:38.046 --> 00:21:40.382
All right. As good as can be. I guess.

324
00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:52.120
Remember coming out here as kids?

325
00:21:52.144 --> 00:21:54.122
Climbing the trees?

326
00:21:54.146 --> 00:21:56.064
Sam would be there scoping for hogs.

327
00:21:57.441 --> 00:22:00.694
- Like he's ever going to see one.
- He pretended a few times.

328
00:22:06.825 --> 00:22:08.660
Well. look at us now?

329
00:22:09.494 --> 00:22:11.848
Peanut M&M's. smoky scotch.

330
00:22:11.872 --> 00:22:15.250
Like kings? Couple of Kirkland kings.

331
00:22:16.293 --> 00:22:17.794
Something like that.

332
00:22:19.421 --> 00:22:22.549
Except I'm not a Kirkland. Never was.

333
00:22:23.383 --> 00:22:24.718
Well. you were to me.

334
00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:27.471
Not to him.

335
00:22:28.305 --> 00:22:29.473
That's why I'm here.

336
00:22:30.932 --> 00:22:31.933
Okay.

337
00:22:32.476 --> 00:22:34.061
Now we're getting somewhere.

338
00:22:34.936 --> 00:22:36.772
He pushed me out of the Double K.

339
00:22:37.814 --> 00:22:38.940
Double K.

340
00:22:39.816 --> 00:22:40.859
God damn.

341
00:22:42.903 --> 00:22:45.214
I used to dream about that place.

342
00:22:45.238 --> 00:22:47.342
Wondered what it looked like
on the inside.

343
00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:50.553
Well. it is part yours. Levi.
You can always come back.

344
00:22:50.577 --> 00:22:51.929
Yeah?

345
00:22:51.953 --> 00:22:55.850
How do you go back somewhere when you
were never welcome in the first place?

346
00:22:55.874 --> 00:22:59.419
Granddad made you a trustee.
You know that. You. you still got say.

347
00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:02.923
What am I going to do with say?

348
00:23:07.344 --> 00:23:08.387
That's it.

349
00:23:10.263 --> 00:23:11.657
You want my say.

350
00:23:11.681 --> 00:23:14.619
Man's running the place into the ground.

351
00:23:14.643 --> 00:23:18.772
But the board votes soon. It could go
either way. You could make the difference.

352
00:23:19.523 --> 00:23:21.167
I know how you feel about this.

353
00:23:21.191 --> 00:23:24.069
That's why I never asked before.
but I'm asking now.

354
00:23:25.654 --> 00:23:27.048
Why?

355
00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:30.510
When he's done with it. there'll
be no trees to climb or trout to catch.

356
00:23:30.534 --> 00:23:32.619
The man is an agent of greed.

357
00:23:33.745 --> 00:23:34.913
And what are you?

358
00:23:37.332 --> 00:23:38.333
I ain't that.

359
00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:58.871
Remember. this guy talks long and smooth.

360
00:23:58.895 --> 00:24:01.541
Might jaw on about weather.
but there's more under it.

361
00:24:01.565 --> 00:24:05.277
You got to meet him. Talk without talking.
You know what I'm saying?

362
00:24:06.069 --> 00:24:08.572
Relax. I got this.

363
00:24:09.364 --> 00:24:10.407
Cheers.

364
00:24:12.033 --> 00:24:13.594
- Whiskey?
- No. ma'am.

365
00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:16.347
I'm not looking for another two-hour nap.

366
00:24:16.371 --> 00:24:17.998
I see Yancy's here. That's nice.

367
00:24:19.207 --> 00:24:20.792
I guess.

368
00:24:21.585 --> 00:24:23.295
His buddy looks high-dollar.

369
00:24:23.795 --> 00:24:25.005
Yeah. not his buddy.

370
00:24:26.923 --> 00:24:28.175
Potential buyer.

371
00:24:31.553 --> 00:24:33.847
- He's selling Fuller?
- Trying to.

372
00:24:34.806 --> 00:24:35.908
Why's he selling?

373
00:24:35.932 --> 00:24:38.185
I don't know. I guess he needs the money.

374
00:24:45.859 --> 00:24:47.962
Youse two are still together.

375
00:24:47.986 --> 00:24:50.089
- Excuse me?
- Not as clever as you think you are.

376
00:24:50.113 --> 00:24:52.216
You're still together.
trying to shake the wife.

377
00:24:52.240 --> 00:24:53.217
Okay.

378
00:24:53.241 --> 00:24:54.451
Shh.

379
00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:56.953
We are.

380
00:24:57.996 --> 00:25:00.349
- She wants money.
- Of course she does.

381
00:25:00.373 --> 00:25:03.102
- No one knows about this.
- Nobody will.

382
00:25:03.126 --> 00:25:05.396
Your secret's safe with me. darling.

383
00:25:05.420 --> 00:25:06.463
Thank you. Sam.

384
00:25:07.297 --> 00:25:08.298
Beer?

385
00:25:08.882 --> 00:25:10.550
Hey. if you twist my arm.

386
00:25:15.263 --> 00:25:16.640
Shoot. …

387
00:25:17.474 --> 00:25:20.036
Got to change the keg.
This might take a sec.

388
00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:21.603
Take your time. darling.

389
00:25:31.029 --> 00:25:32.381
Go time.

390
00:25:32.405 --> 00:25:33.907
And we're standing.

391
00:25:36.618 --> 00:25:38.554
All right. don't forget his tell.

392
00:25:38.578 --> 00:25:42.874
Guy's in a good mood. he refits his hat.
Likes what he's hearing. All right.

393
00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:46.628
Take care. son.
We'll be talking real soon.

394
00:25:51.508 --> 00:25:53.093
That's a nice pair of boots.

395
00:25:54.553 --> 00:25:56.429
These old things?

396
00:25:57.097 --> 00:25:58.157
Sam Kirkland.

397
00:25:58.181 --> 00:25:59.766
- Bob Gaines.
- Pleasure.

398
00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:01.685
Have a seat. Bob Gaines.

399
00:26:07.065 --> 00:26:08.441
You're up. man.

400
00:26:10.068 --> 00:26:11.736
Thought we were playing pool.

401
00:26:12.988 --> 00:26:16.992
Well. just because we're in plain clothes
doesn't mean we're not working.

402
00:26:18.034 --> 00:26:20.245
Stop staring. would you?

403
00:26:21.997 --> 00:26:25.333
So. what are we… what are we working?

404
00:26:26.251 --> 00:26:28.503
Probably something rotten.

405
00:26:29.921 --> 00:26:31.881
No. makes sense.

406
00:26:33.091 --> 00:26:34.360
What?

407
00:26:34.384 --> 00:26:38.739
Nothing. I just thought we were finally
hanging out.

408
00:26:38.763 --> 00:26:40.724
Andrews. man. we are hanging out.

409
00:26:41.224 --> 00:26:42.892
Yeah. I know. I know.

410
00:26:46.313 --> 00:26:47.314
Lucas?

411
00:26:48.148 --> 00:26:51.669
Lucas. Quinn loved the poster.
Like. loved.

412
00:26:51.693 --> 00:26:54.839
It was so sweet.
She. like. lit up when she saw it.

413
00:26:54.863 --> 00:26:57.532
My gosh. It just made me so happy.

414
00:26:58.241 --> 00:26:59.867
Kit. what is happening?

415
00:27:00.994 --> 00:27:05.457
I was trying to take your advice and clear
out the closet. but tiny problem.

416
00:27:06.916 --> 00:27:09.395
Well. actually. a few tiny problems.

417
00:27:09.419 --> 00:27:11.421
My gosh.

418
00:27:12.672 --> 00:27:16.051
Hello. little ones!

419
00:27:17.886 --> 00:27:19.322
Guess it's Mrs. Scratch.

420
00:27:19.346 --> 00:27:21.181
Yeah.

421
00:27:21.765 --> 00:27:24.118
My gosh. I can't!

422
00:27:24.142 --> 00:27:25.244
Can't what?

423
00:27:25.268 --> 00:27:28.146
… I can't deal with your shit is what!

424
00:27:28.772 --> 00:27:32.335
- My goodness. hello.
- Help me get them out of here at least.

425
00:27:32.359 --> 00:27:34.653
My gosh. Don't climb.

426
00:27:35.528 --> 00:27:37.030
Aww. I think he likes you.

427
00:27:38.365 --> 00:27:39.783
My goodness.

428
00:27:55.590 --> 00:27:57.610
Would you drink a ranch water?

429
00:27:57.634 --> 00:27:59.636
They made an extra one back there.

430
00:28:00.762 --> 00:28:02.180
Pop a squat. law man.

431
00:28:07.644 --> 00:28:09.104
So you're Yancy's wife.

432
00:28:10.063 --> 00:28:11.606
He's smart and pretty.

433
00:28:12.107 --> 00:28:13.441
Tell me. where you from?

434
00:28:14.234 --> 00:28:16.253
Everywhere. Where are you from?

435
00:28:16.277 --> 00:28:18.571
Right here.

436
00:28:19.239 --> 00:28:20.239
Scintillating.

437
00:28:21.825 --> 00:28:23.201
How'd you like New Orleans?

438
00:28:25.412 --> 00:28:27.556
I drank a lot of beer in The Spotted Cat.

439
00:28:27.580 --> 00:28:29.892
Yeah. my Aunt Katie B
lived in New Orleans.

440
00:28:29.916 --> 00:28:32.293
Well. she lived in The Spotted Cat.

441
00:28:33.211 --> 00:28:36.005
- I drank a lot of beer there. too.
- Really?

442
00:28:36.506 --> 00:28:38.067
Maybe we crossed paths.

443
00:28:38.091 --> 00:28:39.551
What brought you there?

444
00:28:40.135 --> 00:28:41.904
Roommate in juvie was from NOLA.

445
00:28:41.928 --> 00:28:45.074
So Deputy GQ is a delinquent.

446
00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:46.450
Reformed.

447
00:28:46.474 --> 00:28:47.517
Shame.

448
00:28:48.977 --> 00:28:50.353
I was almost interested.

449
00:28:53.440 --> 00:28:54.899
It was nice meeting you.

450
00:28:55.483 --> 00:28:56.484
Sidney.

451
00:28:57.569 --> 00:28:58.653
Sidney.

452
00:29:02.615 --> 00:29:03.658
Hey.

453
00:29:04.868 --> 00:29:06.536
Don't be a stranger. Kai.

454
00:29:10.790 --> 00:29:14.544
Yeah. that's right. Any records
of Sidney Grey in Dallas or New Orleans.

455
00:29:15.044 --> 00:29:18.882
Bench warrants. parking tickets.
expired licenses. I want all of it.

456
00:29:19.507 --> 00:29:22.635
Hey. while you're at it.
check the name Katie B. too.

457
00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:28.075
One more beer. Sam?

458
00:29:28.099 --> 00:29:29.893
No. thank you. Just water.

459
00:29:30.477 --> 00:29:31.853
Something wrong?

460
00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:35.315
As a matter of fact. there is.

461
00:29:36.191 --> 00:29:38.151
You've been lying through your teeth.

462
00:29:38.735 --> 00:29:42.006
I'm sorry. I don't know
what you're talking about.

463
00:29:42.030 --> 00:29:44.657
Your boyfriend
hasn't been meeting with buyers.

464
00:29:47.577 --> 00:29:48.787
No.

465
00:29:51.956 --> 00:29:53.291
Y'all found oil.

466
00:29:54.083 --> 00:29:55.335
Well. sugar…

467
00:29:57.212 --> 00:29:58.463
I want in.

468
00:30:01.716 --> 00:30:03.778
They're so precious!

469
00:30:03.802 --> 00:30:06.179
- My gosh.
- I know. I can't keep them here.

470
00:30:06.763 --> 00:30:07.806
I know.

471
00:30:08.765 --> 00:30:12.787
Figure our landlord would take one.
and a couple of 'em could be ranch cats.

472
00:30:12.811 --> 00:30:14.705
but I don't want to push it.

473
00:30:14.729 --> 00:30:17.166
That leaves two.

474
00:30:17.190 --> 00:30:18.501
That leaves two.

475
00:30:18.525 --> 00:30:19.585
You want one?

476
00:30:19.609 --> 00:30:20.669
I want five.

477
00:30:20.693 --> 00:30:21.754
Pick one.

478
00:30:21.778 --> 00:30:24.715
No. I can't. It's… It's too much pressure.

479
00:30:24.739 --> 00:30:27.742
Let's just sit here
and look at them a little bit longer.

480
00:30:28.535 --> 00:30:31.287
Okay. You're gonna go see your friends.

481
00:30:34.415 --> 00:30:36.310
Hey. Congrats.

482
00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:38.145
- On what?
- Your poster.

483
00:30:38.169 --> 00:30:39.546
It worked.

484
00:30:40.547 --> 00:30:42.441
Yeah. it did work.

485
00:30:42.465 --> 00:30:44.318
You got a gift. Brigman.

486
00:30:44.342 --> 00:30:48.781
I don't know. I feel like the…
the cowboy really stole the show.

487
00:30:48.805 --> 00:30:52.141
No. His mouth was all messed up.

488
00:30:53.685 --> 00:30:55.770
No. his mouth was perfect.

489
00:31:32.640 --> 00:31:33.808
… I'm…

490
00:31:34.392 --> 00:31:36.936
- I shouldn't… We can't. The…
- Yeah. you're right.

491
00:31:37.437 --> 00:31:39.915
- This didn't happen.
- It didn't happen.

492
00:31:39.939 --> 00:31:41.441
No. No. …

493
00:31:42.775 --> 00:31:44.027
I'm going to leave.

494
00:32:04.047 --> 00:32:05.131
I'm gonna miss this.

495
00:32:07.675 --> 00:32:08.801
Me too.

496
00:32:11.179 --> 00:32:13.640
You know. I never thought
I was going to find you.

497
00:32:15.850 --> 00:32:16.851
But then I did.

498
00:32:18.478 --> 00:32:22.106
And now I have to go my way through life
knowing that you're out there.

499
00:32:24.525 --> 00:32:25.902
When did you know?

500
00:32:32.909 --> 00:32:34.202
Not until today.

501
00:32:38.081 --> 00:32:42.001
I think this is the part where I'm
supposed to say I want you to be happy.

502
00:32:43.461 --> 00:32:44.545
But it's not true.

503
00:32:45.129 --> 00:32:47.423
Because I want you to be happy with me.

504
00:32:53.972 --> 00:32:55.181
I wanted it all.

505
00:32:58.309 --> 00:32:59.686
You'll have all of it.

506
00:33:02.563 --> 00:33:03.773
Just not with me.

507
00:33:05.733 --> 00:33:06.734
Yeah.

508
00:33:08.611 --> 00:33:09.779
Just not with you.

509
00:33:15.535 --> 00:33:16.786
That's me.

510
00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:19.371
Don't try and steal my cab.

511
00:33:44.522 --> 00:33:47.334
<i>Selfishly. part of me.</i>

512
00:33:47.358 --> 00:33:50.129
<i>Wishes there was a part of me.</i>

513
00:33:50.153 --> 00:33:52.756
<i>That could be what you see.</i>

514
00:33:52.780 --> 00:33:55.759
<i>Potentially. everything you want.</i>

515
00:33:55.783 --> 00:33:58.470
<i>Married by a preacher
That we both know.</i>

516
00:33:58.494 --> 00:34:00.806
<i>Least I get to lie awake alone.</i>

517
00:34:00.830 --> 00:34:04.685
<i>Knowing that you're better off
With me long gone</i>

518
00:34:04.709 --> 00:34:07.980
<i>'Cause I loved you enough.</i>

519
00:34:08.004 --> 00:34:11.483
<i>To know I ain't what you'd need.</i>

520
00:34:11.507 --> 00:34:15.738
<i>In the end.</i>

521
00:34:15.762 --> 00:34:19.158
<i>And I left your heart breaking.</i>

522
00:34:19.182 --> 00:34:21.618
<i>When I hit the pavement.</i>

523
00:34:21.642 --> 00:34:26.981
<i>And I'd do it again</i>

524
00:34:28.066 --> 00:34:30.753
<i>'Cause you might hate me now.</i>

525
00:34:30.777 --> 00:34:33.589
<i>But someday. yeah. somehow.</i>

526
00:34:33.613 --> 00:34:38.493
<i>When you find
That someone that ain't me.</i>

527
00:34:39.077 --> 00:34:41.079
<i>You'll see.</i>

528
00:34:41.829 --> 00:34:45.309
<i>That I loved you.</i>

529
00:34:45.333 --> 00:34:48.586
<i>Enough to leave.</i>

530
00:34:52.882 --> 00:34:56.403
<i>Yeah. I loved you.</i>

531
00:34:56.427 --> 00:35:00.223
<i>Enough to leave.</i>

532
00:35:16.781 --> 00:35:19.676
Yeah. he comes out
of the tent in his underwear.

533
00:35:19.700 --> 00:35:21.994
screaming. just hollering.

534
00:35:23.538 --> 00:35:26.791
The fire ants. I forgot about the ants.

535
00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:29.061
Shit.

536
00:35:29.085 --> 00:35:31.045
Why'd it have to be like this?

537
00:35:31.629 --> 00:35:32.922
Like what?

538
00:35:33.798 --> 00:35:35.091
You and I are blood.

539
00:35:36.217 --> 00:35:39.404
We don't live but a few days' ride
and I haven't seen you out here

540
00:35:39.428 --> 00:35:42.116
since I don't know how long.

541
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:44.809
Now you're here asking me for a vote?

542
00:35:46.894 --> 00:35:47.895
For what?

543
00:35:48.646 --> 00:35:49.647
For power?

544
00:35:52.108 --> 00:35:53.693
Money? For land?

545
00:35:57.488 --> 00:36:01.343
Did you ever think it would be like this
when we were kids climbing them trees?

546
00:36:01.367 --> 00:36:02.535
Now. hold on.

547
00:36:04.495 --> 00:36:07.141
I'm sorry.
but there is a war that's waging.

548
00:36:07.165 --> 00:36:09.458
and there is a hell of a lot to lose.

549
00:36:10.168 --> 00:36:12.837
That Double K is my home. It's <i>our</i> home.

550
00:36:13.754 --> 00:36:17.175
If you don't think that's worth
fighting for. then I don't know what is.

551
00:36:19.969 --> 00:36:21.262
<i>Our</i> home?

552
00:36:21.929 --> 00:36:23.681
You gotta be fucking kidding me.

553
00:36:29.103 --> 00:36:32.064
You know. the night my mother died.
I saw an owl.

554
00:36:35.234 --> 00:36:38.112
Massive. white. Flew right over my head.

555
00:36:38.946 --> 00:36:40.406
I took it as a sign.

556
00:36:41.741 --> 00:36:44.785
So I saddled her horse. rode out.

557
00:36:46.704 --> 00:36:47.788
Just rode.

558
00:36:48.289 --> 00:36:49.999
As far north as I could go.

559
00:36:51.209 --> 00:36:52.710
Out into nothing.

560
00:36:55.713 --> 00:36:58.382
And the next morning. I found her.

561
00:36:59.383 --> 00:37:01.177
Sitting on the edge of a lake.

562
00:37:02.094 --> 00:37:04.513
A lake so big.
you couldn't see the other side of it.

563
00:37:09.435 --> 00:37:11.163
I tried to get a little closer.

564
00:37:11.187 --> 00:37:12.438
I didn't want

565
00:37:13.314 --> 00:37:14.523
her to go.

566
00:37:18.569 --> 00:37:19.820
But she flew away.

567
00:37:24.867 --> 00:37:25.952
She flew.

568
00:37:26.744 --> 00:37:27.745
I don't know.

569
00:37:28.412 --> 00:37:29.580
into forever.

570
00:37:32.959 --> 00:37:34.919
Know what your problem is. brother?

571
00:37:37.171 --> 00:37:40.132
You still think home is a place. but it ain't.

572
00:37:41.676 --> 00:37:42.969
Home is a person.

573
00:37:56.023 --> 00:37:58.442
I'll give you your answer in the morning.

574
00:38:43.446 --> 00:38:44.739
Shit.

575
00:38:55.416 --> 00:38:57.102
Hi.

576
00:38:57.126 --> 00:38:58.669
Good morning. deputy.

577
00:38:59.253 --> 00:39:00.254
Trade you.

578
00:39:00.963 --> 00:39:04.568
Nothing on Sidney Grey.
but the boys did get a hit on New Orleans.

579
00:39:04.592 --> 00:39:06.427
One Katheryn Beatrice Lockwood.

580
00:39:07.219 --> 00:39:08.780
Your instinct was right.

581
00:39:08.804 --> 00:39:12.034
Katie B is a person of interest
in an open investigation.

582
00:39:12.058 --> 00:39:13.559
What kind of investigation?

583
00:39:15.102 --> 00:39:16.103
Homicide.

584
00:39:18.147 --> 00:39:19.147
No shit.

585
00:39:20.691 --> 00:39:22.193
Thanks.
